>> looked at the first level:
>> http://bhaak.dyndns.org/nethack/nethack_100x35.png
>>
>> Especially the random corridors are not really nicely put.
>
> What do you think is wrong with the corridors? Looks nice, IMO.

There are a lot of corridors that run alongside walls of a room. Look
for example at those two rooms left of the one with two traps in it.

Then there seems to be a tendency to create unnecessary crossings. At
the center of the screen is a good example for this.


BTW values greater than 128 for COLNO or ROWNO result in a "Floating
exception" crash.

Of course I don't blame the programmer for this.

One of NetHack distinct features is that the level can be seen
completely on the screen (even though it has support for level
scrolling when using big tiles or really small screens). In the past
this meant it had to fit into a 80x24 terminal screen and the level
design is optimized for this size.


These days I play NetHack in a xterm with the font set to 'Huge'.
This is big enough to look good but not that big that I lose the
ability to see the complete level at a glance which is very important
to me.

I have problems playing roguelikes with bigger-than-screen-levels.
Although Crawl for example has a nice random level design I just feel
lost in its huge levels. That is one reason that the only non-nethack
variant I regularly play is DoomRL.


